@bank all
// Writer 5, for social B2: missing someone who moved on. {missed} is their close friend, partner or mentor who has
// left the Wren; the line is skipped for anyone who misses nobody. Light and a little wistful, no #serious. {missed}
// has no known pronouns: name only. Partners only plainly ("I miss {missed}."); nothing that swaps them for you.

== smalltalk
- {missed} would've laughed at that.   #funny
- Still save a seat for {missed}. Habit.
- Letter from {missed} today. Two pages.   #warm
- {missed} always had the last biscuit. Now I do.   #funny
- Wonder what {missed} is having for dinner.
? trad:quiz
- {missed} knew every answer in this round.   #funny
? time:evening
- {missed} would be telling a story about now.

== near
? act:breakfast
- {missed}'s seat's empty. I keep looking at it. Then I eat the toast.
? deck:4 time:night
- {missed}'s old bunk's still made up. Nobody's moved in yet. Odd.
? place:musicroom
- {missed} used to play that one. Badly. I miss it anyway.   #funny
? act:meal
- This was {missed}'s favourite. Still is, probably.

== feel
- I'm all right. Bit quiet without {missed}. You get used to it. Slowly.
- Wrote to {missed} last night. Three pages. Mostly about the food.   #funny
- {missed} says the new ship's fine. Bigger. Colder. Nobody makes tea like Brennan.   #funny
? mood:high
- Good day! {missed} wrote back. Settling in fine, apparently.   #warm
? tier>=friend
- I miss {missed}. Silly, isn't it. It's only one ship over.   #warm
? tier>=friend mood:low
- Missing {missed} today. That's all. Sit a minute? That helps.   #warm

== chat
? tier>=colleague
- {missed} left me a mug. I use it every morning. Don't tell anyone.   #warm
? tier>=friend
- I still save things up to tell {missed}. Then I write them all down. Long letters.
